 **Description:** Running Exp 4307 either writes `blocked_arc_env_unreachable` when the offline ARC environment cannot reset the selected target, writes `complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` when the selected non-`r11l` non-`ls20` non-`wa30` non-`sc25` unattempted game has no verifier-routed real-env level increment in this bounded run, or writes `success: incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total23` only when the offline real environment confirms one new level after the hardened set-encoder route is accepted. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=23`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the selected new game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `verifier_validated=true`, preserve model specs for the offline world-model solver and hardened set-encoder routing, report the selected game/level and why it was selected, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs, preconditions, and trajectory evidence. An honest no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=22`, set `levels_completed=0`, keep `game_advanced` equal to the selected new game id for attribution, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, preserve `target_game` and `target_level`, and still satisfy the acceptance gate when `honest_verdict` is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=22`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, record the failed precondition, and still satisfy the acceptance gate because the verdict is `blocked_arc_env_unreachable`.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-073: ARC-AGI-3 Incremental Progress Exp4317 Adapter-Free Offline Advance
